---
// Strips Rosey tagging from a rendered subtree.
//
// Snippets in a post body are the same page-section components used for page building,
// so they tag their own text with data-rosey. A post body is translated by its per-locale
// content file instead, and the two systems can't share an element: every snippet on the
// page would derive the same key from its `data-prop` (one `heading` for all of them,
// since MDX props carry no `_uuid` to namespace with), and Rosey's substitution would
// then overwrite whatever the locale's content file says.
const html = await Astro.slots.render("default");
---

<Fragment set:html={html.replace(/ data-rosey(?:-[a-z-]+)?="[^"]*"/g, "")} />
